NAME
       rmdir - remove empty directories

SYNOPSIS
       rmdir [-p] [-v] [--ignore-fail-on-non-empty] DIRECTORY...

DESCRIPTION
       rmdir removes directories only when they are empty, which makes it a
       safe choice: it fails with "Directory not empty" instead of deleting
       files. Use rm -r for a directory with files in it.

OPTIONS
       -p, --parents
              Also remove the parent directories that become empty:
              rmdir -p a/b/c removes c, then b, then a.

       -v, --verbose
              Print each directory removed.

       --ignore-fail-on-non-empty
              Do not report directories that are not empty.

EXAMPLES
           rmdir /tmp/empty
           rmdir -p projects/2026/drafts

SEE ALSO
       mkdir(1), rm(1)
